 "text": "The slot holds the head `prototypes + sentences` for `bioclip2-l14` (species_sci, beta 8, bias for species without photos 0.65), fitted on `images/alachua-2025 (two thirds of val)`, with 5911 species rows, and a bias a row. Every photo's vector (`images/alachua-2025`) went through `tools/fusion/fuse.py`, the reference of the page's arithmetic, with the slot's own files as the page reads them (half-precision rows). Settings: rule `product`, t_kind 20, w_kind 0.5, alpha_prior 0.6. On 565 tuning photos (the third of val kept for tuning) the thresholds came out as name_at 0.05 and offer_at never (no level reached nine in ten). On the 4197 test photos the kind of eye is right for 98.6% (98.2 to 98.9); the top species is right for 91.7% (90.9 to 92.6) and is among the first five for 97.6% (97.1 to 98.0). `person` was said for 0.00% of these photos and `none` for 0.00%; the set holds neither. The top species from fuse.py differs from a direct matrix computation on the same files for 0 photos. The kinds head is `kind phrases`. With kind_at 0.20 (set on wildlife tuning photos alone, because the extra set's vectors were not published for this model), the page asserts a kind for 100.0% (99.9 to 100.0) of the wildlife test photos and is right for 98.6% (98.2 to 99.0) of those; for the 0.1% (0.0 to 0.1) where it is not sure, the true kind is among its three likeliest for 50.0% (0.0 to 100.0). The slot needs: species.bias_url (build 7 of the page); fusion.kind_at (the build of the page that has the answer `not sure`).",
